Quick recap
Ukubona and Vincent conducted a meeting to prepare for an upcoming presentation about a digital twin solution for Uganda. They reviewed the key features of the digital twin platform, including district locations, color-coded heat maps, drop-down menus for indicators, data pipelines, and Uganda's data sovereignty. Ukubona provided guidance on how to present the solution effectively, emphasizing the importance of latency reduction in data decision-making and avoiding technical jargon like AI. They discussed how the platform could be expanded to include various indicators beyond health metrics, such as those from Uganda's National Planning Authority's Vision 2040 and national development plans. The meeting focused on highlighting the digital twin's ability to provide real-time data representation and support priority-setting through customizable indicators, with Ukubona suggesting that the platform's value would increase over time as more data and indicators are integrated.
